WEBVTT

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:04.810
Hey.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.320
Is it just me or do we have 
an extra person in our group today?

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.070
It's just you.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:14.930
That's impossible.

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.240
What's this midget doing here?

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.450
What's it got to do with you?

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.140
Masaki-chan came to ask 
me about something...

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.580
she didn't understand in class.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:25.830
Right?

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.880
I just needed some 
 questions clarified.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:31.760
I see.

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:34.880
As I'm top of our grade, I'll tutor you.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.070
I can explain it better than Shun.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:38.890
Let me see.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:40.200
Stop it!

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.150
I want Shun-chan to teach me!

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.170
You're got it all wrong! 
 Kaname, you jerk! Four eyes!

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:50.980
Bookworm!

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.130
Why, you!

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.530
You're not the slightest bit cute.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.360
Masaki-chan's face was red.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.580
Does she have a cold?

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:04.720
Maybe she's lovesick.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:09.600
Maybe she stayed up late studying math.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.120
That's right.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.090
She's desperately trying 
to solve a love equation.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.840
Do you think she went to the hospital?

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.850
You're the one who needs 
to go to the hospital.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:28.180
A transfer student's 
joining our class soon.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:30.690
Apparently, they're 
returning from abroad.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.920
Really?

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:36.240
There's been a lot of 
activity around us lately.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:41.490
We met an awkward first year,

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:45.600
and now a meeting an unknown 
transfer student awaits us.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:20.210
I'd like to introduce a transfer student.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.890
I'm Chizuru Tachibana.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.110
Nice to meet you.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.390
If you have any questions,

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:30.350
ask your class representative, 
Tsukahara-kun.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.410
Tachibana-kun, your desk is over there.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:35.560
Okay.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:38.520
Nice to meet you.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:41.210
I hope you'll share your 
textbook when I forget mine.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.820
Nice to meet you, too.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:46.340
Charmed.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.510
I'm taking attendance.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:53.330
Aoto.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:53.880
Here.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:54.710
Akaishi.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:55.300
Here.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:56.200
Akiyama.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:56.910
Here.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.520
What a shock!

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.560
You're that kid, aren't you?

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.130
No, um...

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.130
Tachibana-kun...

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:12.110
We played together at that park!

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:12.910
Didn't we?

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.810
That was such a long time ago.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:17.150
Small world, huh?

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:18.310
Right?

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:20.640
Who are you?

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:29.660
What's wrong?

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.170
You're here every break.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:36.570
Someone keeps making strange 
advances if I'm over there.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:41.670
How unusual for someone 
to approach you head on.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.790
It's not so much head 
on as from the right.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.180
Found you!

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:51.990
A clone?

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:54.120
We're twins.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.910
I'm his older brother, Yuta.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:00.570
Oh, you're just his twin brother.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.070
How do you two know each other?

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:06.630
In his delusional world, we 
used to know each other.

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:08.770
That's not it!

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.670
We really do know each other!

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:12.830
There you are.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:16.280
I thought I'd give you 
a tour of the school.

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:17.530
Are you free?

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.280
Who are you?

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:23.820
Kaname Tsukahara. I'm in your class.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:27.400
Our teacher told you to come to 
me if you have any questions.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:30.050
I'll ask Yukki, so don't sweat it.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:32.030
Yukki?

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:36.200
He calls you Yukki?

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:40.380
We're old friends, so it's 
an affectionate nickname.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:46.570
I'll affectionately call you, my classmate...

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:47.950
Four eyes.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:51.630
That name's clearly full of animosity.

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:52.790
Now, now...

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:55.890
You two must be friends.

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:59.060
First thing you do is piss me off.

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.750
Birds of a feather flock together.

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:06.760
But Yuki's acting like he's got 
him confused with someone else.

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:11.330
A stranger's a stranger. See you later.

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:13.100
What's wrong with you?

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:15.710
He's so cold.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.970
I feel like he used to be a lot nicer.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.630
Nice?

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.480
You've definitely got the wrong guy.

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:26.780
I'm sure he's just embarrassed 
to see his old friend again.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.780
I've got to make Yukki acknowledge me!

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:32.470
Hold up, Yu—

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.500
Who's that? His girlfriend?

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:46.250
That's not his girlfriend.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:47.970
He's not even a girl.

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:49.980
How dare you say that?!

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:52.680
I know she's a little flat chested,

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:57.180
but it's our job as men 
to appreciate them anyway!

00:06:58.070 --> 00:06:59.980
Hey, girlfriend!

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.000
Where did they go?

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.220
Hey, hey, hey.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:08.070
I said he's not a girl.

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:15.100
Yuta, words are meaningless 
until the other person listens.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:22.290
He's not a girl.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.540
There you go again, saying the 
same thing as your brother.

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.890
That girl was so cute.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:31.430
What a shame I didn't 
get to talk to her.

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:35.720
Not that I was afraid 
of being shot down.

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:38.970
She seemed to be heading 
to the locker room.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:43.090
Amazing. Did you see that?

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:46.820
Hey.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.490
You really don't remember me?

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:54.490
More like...

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.540
I have no idea who you are.

00:07:56.890 --> 00:08:00.040
Girls don't like 
overly persistent guys.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.090
But you're a boy...

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:14.510
I was wondering who you were.

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:18.030
I didn't recognize you right 
away without your glasses.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:23.290
I thought you were Yuta 
with your hair like that.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.790
Oh, my bangs.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.480
Wait!

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:40.290
Who are you?

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.420
I told you...

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.790
Hey, that kid you played with once...

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.210
You remember?

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.710
Could it have been Yuta?

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:50.890
What?

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:54.220
You've got us confused. 
We look the same.

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:57.810
You are identical, but...

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:02.320
I'm pretty sure it was Yukki.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:14.700
Still not done?

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:16.200
Not yet.

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:18.690
You're just going to 
end up buying it.

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:21.840
I won't know if it's worth buying a copy...

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:24.140
for archival purposes until I've read it.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:26.920
You should stop doing that.

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:31.340
Books are made to be read.

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:36.900
You're not telling me you know 
how this book feels, do you?

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:38.820
I do understand.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:40.270
Now, hurry up and buy it.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.640
Now I'm kind of jealous.

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:45.990
I'll  keep reading until I understand it, too.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:48.520
That's not what I wanted.

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:53.280
That kid really is blond, isn't he?

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:57.400
From far away, he looks like 
he's wearing a straw hat.

00:09:57.770 --> 00:09:59.620
Could it have been Yuta?

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:02.370
I've got to find a way...

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:07.450
This one again?

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:12.000
This...

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:14.800
If you're going to buy 
it, just buy it already.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:18.090
I can always buy manga volumes later,

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:21.120
but it's hard to find magazines 
long after they've been published.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:24.560
Hold on.

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:27.560
Did you follow us?

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:30.480
Do you remember the toy I gave you?

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:31.360
What toy?

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.730
I gave you one!

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:36.210
I don't remember what it was, 
but I'm sure it was cool.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:37.200
Who knows?

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.610
"Who knows?"

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:41.020
I did! I gave it to you!

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:42.600
Yeah, but...

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.860
Was this in front of the park?

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:51.960
My memory's pretty fuzzy, so 
I don't remember the details.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:55.460
I think someone gave me 
something like that.

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:57.510
What? Then...

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:01.310
Oh, but I don't remember you.

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:11.690
What?

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.230
I see. So it was Yuta.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:16.310
I don't remember him at all, though.

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:18.780
What are you talking about?

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:22.660
At least he's stopped bothering you.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:23.660
Right?

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:25.870
So small.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.200
Who are you guys talking about?

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:29.920
That's all for today.

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:33.460
Students on day duty please bring 
the daybook to the faculty office later.

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:08.860
Everyone I ask says they 
don't remember me.

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:12.220
Maybe I'm actually a fictional character.

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:15.990
What're you laughing at, huh?

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:17.380
Um...

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:20.180
You just smirked at us, didn't you?

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:22.570
No, I...

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:28.560
You're too cocky for a nobody.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.560
What's with this hair?

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:33.310
You think this blond hair looks cool?

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:36.190
Don't get so excited over this crap.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:46.410
You bastard!

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:49.090
What are you doing?

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:53.410
Yutan and Yukki.

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:55.510
What do you want?

00:12:55.510 --> 00:12:58.040
There sure are a lot of you 
against just one opponent.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:01.300
No, no. That's not what this is.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:02.420
I was just playing around.

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:06.010
Who do you think you are?

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:08.010
Say something!

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:10.230
I'm finished.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:12.530
Where's the second volume?

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:17.980
Huh? Um, in my bag or my locker or...

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:22.030
What? How am I supposed 
to know from that?

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:25.360
Let me borrow this guy for a minute.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:27.550
What are you talking about?

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:29.490
I'll return him later.

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:30.200
Let's go!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.600
Wait!

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:33.250
He's busy with...

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:33.250
It's the Principal.

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:34.970
Let's go!

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:37.000
Hey, wait!

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:16.180
I'm bored.

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:20.320
It's summer, but Yuta's sick.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:22.530
What am I going to do by myself?

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:31.260
His head's yellow, like a straw hat.

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:36.390
What language is that?

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.400
You want to play together?

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:49.650
Um, what's your name?

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:53.450
My mom told me not to 
talk to strangers.

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:57.910
He doesn't understand me.

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:05.350
Another nobody.

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:08.000
Do you want to try?

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:11.360
Put it in.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:15.990
And turn it.

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:26.110
Hero Yamato complete version!

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:32.110
No, I've got to get it myself.

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:38.040
More importantly, why am I 
here with some stranger kid...

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:47.880
I don't mind playing 
without talking, though.

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:50.800
Wait!

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:54.260
Oh, no.

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:56.450
Sorry.

00:15:57.360 --> 00:16:01.020
You've done it now, you jerk.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.930
Now it's my turn.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:20.950
<i>Almost there.</i>

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:13.980
Um...

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:20.200
Wait here.

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:24.440
I'll go get an adult.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:43.870
Sorry.

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:51.980
I guess he can't understand 
even if I apologize.

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:04.670
Yuta-chan's finally better, 
and now you're sick.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:06.540
Where's Yuta?

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:09.610
He's out shopping.

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:14.150
It's a shame you can't play outside 
in this beautiful weather.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:17.830
It's fine.

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:30.710
<i>What does he want?</i>

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:53.940
I'm home.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:57.760
I bought some apple juice.

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:00.040
Thanks.

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:03.960
And I got you a gift.

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.780
Hero Yamato.

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:09.490
No fair, Yuta. You 
used the toy machine?

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:11.280
No.

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:15.780
When I passed by the park,

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:20.720
this yellow-haired kid came 
up to me and gave me this.

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:24.340
I couldn't understand 
anything he said, though.

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:29.770
I'm not interested in that 
stuff, so you can have it.

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:32.860
Yuki?

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:38.330
<i>I wanted to get it myself...</i>

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:44.780
My words melted in that childlike 
light without reaching him.

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:50.330
Only the blue summer 
sky saw what happened.

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:15.230
Yukki, you were the one 
I played with that day.

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:22.790
You should just say it was Yuta.

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:30.010
You and Yutan aren't clones.

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:33.910
You read manga in the face of violence.

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:40.170
And I don't apologize 
for hurting others.

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:42.130
You don't?

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:44.470
I'm talking about what happened to you.

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:47.720
Oh, that.

00:20:49.070 --> 00:20:54.940
I guess it did hurt, but I wouldn't 
have wanted you to apologize.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:59.500
I really had fun.

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:05.790
I had fun and I was happy, so 
an apology is a little...

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:08.480
Right?

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:22.240
I wouldn't learn German 
just to apologize.

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:24.580
It'd be too much work.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:35.310
Hey.

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:38.810
Is it just me, or do we have 
another extra member today?

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:40.690
Her name's Matsuoka-san?

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:42.900
Your girlfriend is cute, isn't she?

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:46.520
I heard she's good friends with all 
of you and usually comes up here.

00:21:46.920 --> 00:21:48.720
Who's Matsuoka-san?

00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:50.240
Furthermore, who are you?

00:21:52.100 --> 00:21:53.750
I thought you'd be here.

00:21:54.430 --> 00:21:56.170
It's Matsuoka-san.

00:21:58.400 --> 00:22:00.250
Matsuoka-san...

00:22:02.110 --> 00:22:03.510
You're late.

00:22:03.780 --> 00:22:06.320
I had to fill in the daybook.

00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:14.060
Yes?

00:22:16.290 --> 00:22:18.700
Nice to meet you, Matsuoka-kun.

00:22:18.700 --> 00:22:21.060
Nice to meet you.

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:24.820
Hey.

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:27.470
Are you okay?

00:22:27.470 --> 00:22:29.820
Don't wake him, Shun.

00:22:30.050 --> 00:22:34.110
Don't ever wake him. He never shuts up.

00:22:34.110 --> 00:22:36.460
I tried to tell him you weren't a girl.

00:22:36.460 --> 00:22:39.790
Words really are powerful things.

